[metal] Add a toggle to survive MTLCommandBufferErrorNotPermitted

iOS fails command buffers committed, or not yet scheduled, while the
application is in the background with MTLCommandBufferErrorNotPermitted:
GPU access is restricted there, but the device itself stays usable. Dawn
154 did not look at a completed command buffer's status, so the refused
work was simply lost and rendering went on. Since Dawn 157 the completed
handler in QueueMTL.mm treats every failure as an execution error and
loses the device, so an app with GPU work in flight when it goes to the
background comes back to a lost device (#4290). WebKit's WebGPU makes the
distinction in Source/WebGPU/WebGPU/Queue.mm, where only an error other
than MTLCommandBufferErrorNotPermitted loses the device.

With the metal_ignore_not_permitted_command_buffer_errors toggle enabled,
the work of such a command buffer is discarded, its serial advances as if
it had completed, and a warning is logged from the next submit (the handler
runs on a Metal thread and cannot call into the device). Resources the
discarded work wrote keep their previous, possibly uninitialized, contents.
The toggle is off by default: device creation has to opt in.

Upstream: https://github.com/google/dawn/pull/91. The PR also adds
MetalBackendTests cases for both behaviours, left out here because the
monolithic build does not compile the tests.

Drop this patch when the pinned Dawn carries the toggle.

